p-refusal.text:
Add a tiny “AllocationResult” value object:

```java
public final class AllocationResult {
    private final Spot spot;          // null when none
    private final boolean success;   // false → no spot
    private final String reason;     // optional diagnostic

    private AllocationResult(Spot s, boolean ok, String r) {
        this.spot = s; this.success = ok; this.reason = r;
    }
    public static AllocationResult ok(Spot s)   { return new AllocationResult(s,true,null); }
    public static AllocationResult fail(String r){ return new AllocationResult(null,false,r); }
    // getters …
}
```

Change the strategy API to `AllocationResult selectSpot(Vehicle v, List<Spot> candidates)`.  
`DefaultAllocation` walks the list; if it finds a fit it returns `AllocationResult.ok(found)`, otherwise `AllocationResult.fail("no "+v.type()+" spot")`.  

`Floor.findSpot` just forwards the result.  
`ParkingLot.enter` checks `result.isSuccess()`. On failure it builds `EntryResult` with `refused=true` and the supplied reason, never returns a raw `null`. This makes the “no‑spot” case explicit and type‑safe.
